%% API interrupt / resume flow — any frontend
sequenceDiagram
  participant C1 as ClientA
  participant Gw as Gateway
  participant O as LangGraph
  participant CP as Checkpointer
  participant C2 as ClientB_or_same
  participant A as ApprovalOptional
  C1->>Gw: POST threads
  Gw-->>C1: thread_id
  C1->>Gw: POST runs input StartRun
  Gw->>O: ainvoke input thread_id
  O->>CP: checkpoint steps
  O->>O: interrupt payload
  CP-->>O: persist interrupted snapshot
  O-->>Gw: __interrupt__
  Gw-->>C1: RunResult awaiting_* + InterruptPayload
  Note over C1,C2: Frontend may disconnect; STM stays in checkpointer
  C2->>Gw: GET threads/id/state
  Gw->>O: get_state
  O-->>Gw: StateSnapshot
  Gw-->>C2: RuntimeState DTO + messages preview
  C2->>Gw: POST approvals or ResumeRun command.resume
  Gw->>A: record Approval if required
  A-->>Gw: ok
  Gw->>O: ainvoke Command resume same thread_id
  Note over O: node re-enters; pre-interrupt code re-runs idempotently
  O->>CP: continue checkpoints
  O-->>Gw: output or next interrupt
  Gw-->>C2: RunResult
